# cd (roadmap os-server.md P9): relative and absolute, "." and "..", a
# drive DOS's way and in any case, and HOME without an argument; a file or
# a missing name is no directory, and "/.." is "/". One current directory
# for all the drives, as POSIX has it, not DOS's one a drive; each of its
# names in its own case, as the server or FAT has it.
program: sh
emulators: bochs mame
keys: cd c:/; pwd; cd docs; cd .; pwd; cd ..; pwd; cd /c/docs/../docs; pwd\n
keys: cd /D; pwd; cd B:/MANY; pwd; cd ..; cd readme.txt; cd nowhere\n
keys: cd /; cd ..; pwd; cd; pwd\n
---
rx286, test build
/a$ cd c:/; pwd; cd docs; cd .; pwd; cd ..; pwd; cd /c/docs/../docs; pwd
/c
/c/DOCS
/c
/c/DOCS
/c/DOCS$ cd /D; pwd; cd B:/MANY; pwd; cd ..; cd readme.txt; cd nowhere
/d
/b/MANY
sh: readme.txt: not a directory
sh: nowhere: no such file or directory
/b$ cd /; cd ..; pwd; cd; pwd
/
/a
/a$
